# E066 · Learning Enough to Disagree

[Essay catalogue](../README.md) · [Original manuscript](original.md)

## How this essay was made

Part of the twenty-essay plain-language experiment. A fresh author wrote a draft, a separate critic examined it, and the author revised. The prose instruction aimed for simple human language while preserving the argument. Later essays in this batch changed models during production; exact observations are retained below.

Campaign: `plain20-20260910` · Lineage: `essay-43`. The midterm ID is a blinded corpus label, not a rank.

Recorded model observations: `gpt-6-astra`, `gpt-6-astra / low`. These identify recorded configurations, not independent backend attestation.

